\subsection{Offline evaluation}\label{sec:offline}
It is important to note that the baseline made 11 errors and the adapted method made 8 errors on the same 120-query set. The mean latency was 310 ms for the baseline and 345 ms for the adapted method; these values do not establish a population-level difference \citep{lee:offline}.

\subsection{Reproducibility}\label{sec:repro}
We used seed 17, jitter \(10^{-8}\), a tolerance of \(10^{-6}\), and at most 4 retries in \texttt{solve\_retry.py}. Under Assumption A, \(f(x)\leq B\) for \(x\in S\); \eqref{eq:bound} states the bound.

